CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ static_cast void\* -> const function-pointer\*: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [expr.static.cast]/13, [conv.qual]: static_cast from a (cv) void* to a
pointer-to-T is valid when the target is at least as cv-qualified.  This must
hold when T is a function pointer (const void* -> const FP*).
cast_away_constness now special-cases a void* source symmetrically to a void*
target, so the (valid) cast is accepted.  Underlies std::function's
_Base_manager::_M_get_pointer.
